# Copy this file to .env and paste your EDB subscription token before building.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# EDB_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKEN is the ONLY secret you need. It is used as a Docker build
# secret to build the PGD/PGAA image (pgd/) from EDB's package repositories — it is
# never baked into an image, and .env is git-ignored. Every other credential in the
# repo is a local Docker default (see demo-config.toml) for services bound to
# localhost only.
#
# Get a free token:
#   1. Sign up for a free EDB account at https://www.enterprisedb.com/
#   2. Open "EDB Repos 2.0" / repository access in your account and copy the token
#   3. Paste it below
#
# The non-EDB components (Kafka, Kafka Connect, MinIO, Lakekeeper, ClickHouse,
# DuckDB) use public images and need no token. WarehousePG (whpg/, optional) builds
# from a prebaked EDB base image that is not public — it is off the critical path
# and `make up` does not start it; see README "Notes & known limitations".
EDB_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKEN=your-edb-subscription-token-here

# Which Dockerfile builds the PGD/PGAA image. Leave as the default unless you have a
# prebaked EDB base image in your local Docker cache and a matching Dockerfile.
PGD_DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile
